<       - alert: BackupFreshnessStaleWeekly
<         # MON-GAP-018: per-job freshness for the weekly host backups published by the
<         # lane box (backup-freshness-stamp.sh -> node-exporter-textfile/backup-freshness.prom).
<         # 1.5x the weekly schedule = 10.5d. job=cube-agent with value 0 = no complete
<         # MANIFEST ever found in its S3 prefix (also the failure mode).
<         expr: |
<           (time() - monitoring_backup_last_success_timestamp_seconds{exported_job=~"kara-hermes|cube-agent"}) > 907200
<         for: 30m
<         labels:
<           severity: warning
<           lane: monitoring
<         annotations:
<           summary: "weekly backup job {{ $labels.job }} has no successful upload in 10.5d"
<           description: |
<             The weekly host backup job {{ $labels.job }} (s3://dexdat-backups) has not
<             completed a verified upload (MANIFEST present) for over 10.5 days.
<             value 0 means no manifest was ever found for that job.
<           runbook: docs/runbook.md#backup-stale
<       - alert: InventorySweepStale
<         # textfile-collector metric: if the sweep stops publishing, the metric goes
<         # absent — absence is the failure mode, same pattern as BackupFreshnessStale.
<         expr: |
<           (time() - fleet_inventory_last_success_timestamp_seconds) > 604800
<         for: 1h
<         labels:
<           severity: warning
<           lane: monitoring
<         annotations:
<           summary: "fleet software inventory sweep has not run for 7d"
<           description: |
<             The scheduled fleet inventory sweep (MON-GAP-007) has not published a fresh
<             inventory for over a week. Drift (new containers, dead agents, unreachable
<             hosts) is no longer being observed.
<           runbook: docs/runbook.md#inventory-sweep-is-stale
